Nothing remarkable about the game. Like in all my successful games, I
used my early magic lamp as a light source. Got BoH from a throne;
didn't use any other wishes. Main weapons Excalibur, Frost Brand and a
silver saber (alternating them).

Made only one stupid mistake: dug down on Orcus' level to save time,
without understanding that the pit would be filled with water (the way
it was positioned). Blanked my stack of blessed ?oRC that way.
Fortunately I didn't need it; I had very few problems with random
cursing -- about as few as I normally have as a Wizard wielding
Magicbane. Had few Rodney problems in general; I killed him 9 times
mostly with /oDeath.

One thing: robe + spell of magic missile -- what's up with that? Even
at basic skill it seemed incredibly powerful. One zap could take out a
balrog. Normally I regard missile as almost useless in the later game
and only use it on large numbers of weak monsters, like summoned bugs.

As usual, the third and last altar was mine. I had to kill Famine four
times, Pestilence twice and Death once. Had a few close calls
meanwhile, before I learned to teleport monsters out of my way and
to block the Riders with harmless or sleeping monsters.

